# FABLE-L2-ARG-ADDRESS-PROOF-20260921-84.  THE ONE BOUNDARY: a dynamic input whose source has no value cell.
#
# `leaf` reads the free name `label`; its caller has a formal of that name, so a source EXISTS --
# but its type (a const LmP0Text) has no value cell a dynamic input could travel through.  That is
# refused at the caller, by name: "dynamic input type has no value cell".  Before, the same
# program was refused at `leaf` as an "unresolved name", as if nobody had supplied `label` at all.
fn: leaf () int
    if: label = 0
        return: 1
    return: 0
end: leaf
fn: outer (const: @(LmP0Text label)) int
    return: leaf()
end: outer
return: 0
